  "description": "In a library an importer can hold a value of any type the exported API carries, through a parameter, a result, a field, an element, a method of a type the API reaches, an alias or a pointer, and code outside the analyzed program may make a value of it by any number. A member whose deletion renumbers a named member of such a type is retained, and an exported constant of an importable package counts as named because an importer can name it. A member after the last named one moves nothing when deleted and is reported, and so is a member of a type no exported declaration holds whose values are only compared.",
